<section aria-labelledby="before">
  <h2 id="before">Before</h2>
  <ol class="timeline">
    <li class="tl-item">
      <details class="tl" id="tl-0">
        <summary>
          <span class="tl-years">2020–2026</span>
          <span class="tl-org">Dirigo Insights</span>
          <span class="tl-role">Founder</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <p>I grew Dirigo to two employees and seven contractors, and we worked with more than 30 education companies, school groups, and investors on what schools need, what to build or buy, and how to make it work in classrooms. Much of that work came during the science of reading boom, when many literacy companies changed hands.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <details class="tl" id="tl-1">
        <summary>
          <span class="tl-years">2021–2024</span>
          <span class="tl-org">Really Great Reading</span>
          <span class="tl-role">Consultant, then Chief Operating Officer</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <p>The founders brought me in as a consultant, then asked me to stay on as COO. Working alongside them, I focused on technical compliance, product management and strategy, large district implementation, and the due diligence behind the company's acquisition by The Vistria Group in 2022.</p>
          <div class="srcs">
            <a class="src" href="https://www.reallygreatreading.com">reallygreatreading.com</a>
            <a class="src" href="https://vistria.com/the-vistria-group-announces-strategic-partnership-with-leading-literacy-firm-really-great-reading/">Vistria announcement, Dec 2022</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <details class="tl" id="tl-2">
        <summary>
          <span class="tl-years">2013–2019</span>
          <span class="tl-org">Cambium Learning Group</span>
          <span class="tl-role">Learning A-Z, corporate, and Voyager Sopris Learning</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <p>When Cambium acquired Headsprout in 2013, I joined Learning A-Z as an implementation consultant. Over the next six years I moved from implementation to R&amp;D to leading two of Cambium's businesses, and worked on its acquisitions along the way.</p>
          <ol class="arc">
            <li>
              <span class="arc-h">
                <a class="arc-name" href="https://www.learninga-z.com">Learning A-Z</a>
                <span class="role">Consultant → Sr. Director, Implementation → VP, R&amp;D → President</span>
              </span>
              <p>Starting as a consultant, I led pilot implementations in several of the largest U.S. districts and built the professional services approach that served our growing international customer base. In R&amp;D, what implementation taught us went back into the products. As president, I led Cambium's largest division, serving more than 5 million students in over 170 countries, as annual bookings grew past <span class="num">$80 million</span>.</p>
              <div class="srcs">
                <a class="src" href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1466815/000146681518000016/abcd12311710-k.htm">Cambium 10-K, FY2017 (SEC)</a>
                <a class="src" href="https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2017/12/28/1275662/34357/en/Cambium-Learning-Group-Appoints-Patrick-Marcotte-President-of-Learning-A-Z.html">Appointment, Dec 2017</a>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="arc-h">
                <span class="arc-name">Acquisitions</span>
                <span class="role">Cambium corporate</span>
              </span>
              <p>Cambium acquired Time4Learning in 2018 and AIR's assessment division the next year, and I was part of the team behind both. AIR's division had delivered about 60 million online tests across more than 20 states and became Cambium Assessment. I also served on the Sarbanes-Oxley compliance team while Cambium was public, until Veritas Capital took it private.</p>
              <div class="srcs">
                <a class="src" href="https://www.edsurge.com/news/2019-08-22-cambium-buys-assessment-division-of-nonprofit-air">AIR deal, Aug 2019</a>
                <a class="src" href="https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20200106005329/en/Cambium-Learning-Group-Completes-Its-Acquisition-of-Assessment-Division-of-the-American-Institutes-for-Research">AIR close, Jan 2020</a>
                <a class="src" href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001466815/000119312518298772/d619120dex991.htm">Veritas merger, Oct 2018 (SEC)</a>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="arc-h">
                <a class="arc-name" href="https://www.voyagersopris.com">Voyager Sopris Learning</a>
                <span class="role">President, including Kurzweil Education</span>
              </span>
              <p>The big bet was focusing the business on LETRS, its science of reading professional development for teachers, which is now the teacher-training standard in 23 states. <a href="https://www.kurzweiledu.com">Kurzweil Education</a>, accessibility software for students with learning differences, was slated to be wound down. Instead, I led the team that returned it to growth.</p>
              <div class="srcs">
                <a class="src" href="https://www.globenewswire.com/en/news-release/2019/09/12/1914600/0/en/Schools-districts-states-nationwide-increasingly-turning-to-Voyager-Sopris-Learning-s-LETRS-professional-development.html">LETRS release, Sept 2019</a>
                <a class="src" href="https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2019/11/19/1949238/0/en/Cambium-Learning-Group-Appoints-Innovative-Executive-to-Lead-Its-Largest-Division.html">Move to Voyager Sopris, Nov 2019</a>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <details class="tl" id="tl-3">
        <summary>
          <span class="tl-years">2009–2013</span>
          <span class="tl-org">Headsprout</span>
          <span class="tl-role">Graduate intern to implementation lead</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <p>Headsprout made adaptive early reading software. I started as a graduate intern gathering user feedback on its new Reading Comprehension product in Chicago Public Schools, then implemented Headsprout in large districts across the U.S. I led the business through its acquisition by Cambium Learning Group in 2013.</p>
          <div class="srcs">
            <a class="src" href="https://www.skyviewcapital.com/learning-a-z-acquires-headsprout-instructional-software-unit-from-skyview-capital">Acquisition announcement, Dec 2013</a>
            <a class="src" href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/headsprout-showcases-award-winning-literacy-programs-at-2012-national-title-i-conference-137748553.html">Nashville case study, 2012</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <details class="tl" id="tl-4">
        <summary>
          <span class="tl-years">2005–2008</span>
          <span class="tl-org">Psychiatric care and classrooms</span>
          <span class="tl-role">Tech, then paraprofessional</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <p>My first jobs were overnight and school-day shifts at a state psychiatric hospital in Maine. During graduate school in Chicago, I worked as a paraprofessional serving children with autism and provided in-home support.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

